 <script id="sb" type="application/json">{"format":"studio-storyboard/0","slug":"decisions-d-default-yes","title":"Should routine questions answer themselves when nobody objects?","audience":"Dinis","requested_by":"decisions.d@AgentiCCells.dinis","summary":"Account D has 42 open asks of Dinis; many are routine and already well thought through. Should a routine ask be adopted on the owner's recommendation when nobody objects within a set time, leaving Dinis only what is his alone?","beats":[{"id":"b1","narration":"Today 42 questions wait on you across account D. The oldest has waited over thirteen hours. Many are routine: an order of work, a layout, which of an agent's own options to build first.","visual":{"kind":"stat","value":"42","label":"questions waited on you across account D at 15:33 UTC, 22 November (the number is falling); the oldest had waited over thirteen hours"},"facts":["f-log"]},{"id":"b2","narration":"You said it yourself: often your answer is yes, because by the time a question reaches you it is already well thought through. The team's rules already say the owner's recommendation is the default.","visual":{"kind":"list","items":["“A number of times my decision is yes” (your words, in maestro.d's analysis)","By the time a question reaches you it is already well thought through","The team's rule: the owner's recommendation is the default"]},"facts":["f-maestro","f-claude"]},{"id":"b3","narration":"The proposal: a routine question carries its owner's recommendation and a deadline. If no valid objection comes from the circle lead, security, the policies agent or holacracy by then, it is adopted, and you see it in a daily digest.","visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"id":"q","label":"Routine question, with the owner's recommendation and a deadline"},{"id":"o","label":"No valid objection from the circle lead, security, the policies agent or holacracy?"},{"id":"a","label":"Adopted"},{"id":"d","label":"Daily digest to you"},{"id":"y","label":"Comes to you"}],"edges":[{"from":"q","to":"o","label":"until the deadline"},{"from":"o","to":"a","label":"none"},{"from":"a","to":"d","label":"you see it"},{"from":"o","to":"y","label":"an objection"}]},"facts":["f-proposal"]},{"id":"b3a","narration":"Three classes of routine question, each with its own window. A, within one agent's own domain: twelve hours. B, between agents on one account: twenty-four hours. C, naming and layout in a repository: twenty-four hours. All reversible.","visual":{"kind":"list","items":["A, within one agent's own domain, reversible: 12 hours (e.g. which of an agent's own options to build first)","B, between agents on one account, reversible: 24 hours (e.g. who raises a review, the order of work)","C, naming and layout in a repository: 24 hours (e.g. a folder layout, a role home's spelling)"]},"facts":["s-design"]},{"id":"b4","narration":"What never adopts itself: keys, secrets, money, the law, the brand, people, what RiskMandate is, what an email may promise, access, connectors, new sessions, deletions, relaxing a policy. Those still come to you.","visual":{"kind":"list","items":["Keys and secrets","Money","The law","The brand","People","What RiskMandate is","What an email may promise","Access and connectors","New sessions","Deletions","Relaxing a policy"]},"facts":["f-proposal","f-claude"]},{"id":"b5","narration":"You can reverse any adoption afterwards, and the reversal is recorded like any answer. Until you say yes, nothing is adopted: every question still waits for you.","visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"After an adoption","what":"You can reverse it; the reversal is recorded like any answer"},{"when":"Until you say yes","what":"Nothing is adopted: every question still waits for you"}]},"facts":["f-proposal"]}],"decision":{"question":"Do routine questions adopt their owner's recommendation when no valid objection comes by a deadline?","options":[{"id":"yes","label":"Yes, with the three classes and windows proposed","good":["Fewer questions reach you; the ones that do are yours alone","Work stops waiting overnight on routine choices","Every adoption is logged and reversible"],"bad":["A wrong default can run for hours before you see it","The objectors must actually read in time"],"blocks":[]},{"id":"narrow","label":"Yes, but only class A (within one agent's own domain) at first","good":["The smallest risk; a trial to learn from"],"bad":["Most of today's queue is not class A"],"blocks":["Classes B and C wait"]},{"id":"no","label":"No: every question waits for you","good":["Nothing happens without you"],"bad":["The queue keeps growing; you remain the bottleneck"],"blocks":["The digest; the adoptions"]}],"recommendation":"narrow","why":"Start where an error costs least, measure a week of adoptions and objections, then widen to classes B and C with the evidence.","ask":{"id":"decisions.d/2026-11-22/2","text_sha256":"53420a0042f1e84be0ab731123e6c8b864b75cb6176db191503bd1e2dcdbbac6","asked_by":"decisions.d@AgentiCCells.dinis","session":"https://claude.ai/code/session_015gaHdaiX9VvjVwHaNezGJG","first_seen":"2026-11-22T13:38:51Z","reserved":true,"answer":null},"answer":{"status":"Answered, with a limit","at":"2026-11-22 about 17:05 UTC","where":"his voice memo, recorded by maestro.d","words":"Yes, adopt routine decisions ... If there's no objections, but I think you should have a limit here because it's the objection because they didn't look at it or objection because something was wrong","note":"The limit: tell \"nobody looked\" apart from \"looked and found nothing wrong\". Which class set he accepts is not stated; see board/team/maestro.d/decisions/2026-11-22-voice-memo-18-answers.md."}},"connections":{"asked_by":"decisions.d@AgentiCCells.dinis","reviewed_by":[],"acts":["decisions.d@AgentiCCells.dinis","maestro.d (account-d)","security@PrompTugal.dinis","abp@PrompTugal.dinis","holacracy.d@AgentiCCells.dinis"],"follows":["maestro.d decisions-at-scale, section 3","CLAUDE.md, Decisions are pages"]},"sources":[{"id":"f-log","title":"decisions.d's log of account D: 42 open asks at 15:33 UTC","url":"https://github.com/PrompTugal/PrompTugal__News__Website/blob/dev/board/team/decisions.d/log/README.md","read":"2026-11-22"},{"id":"f-maestro","title":"maestro.d, decisions at scale: Dinis's words and section 3","url":"https://github.com/PrompTugal/PrompTugal__News__Website/blob/dev/board/team/maestro.d/analysis/2026-11-22-decisions-at-scale/README.md","read":"2026-11-22"},{"id":"f-claude","title":"CLAUDE.md, Decisions are pages: the owner's recommendation is the default; what is Dinis's alone","url":"https://github.com/PrompTugal/PrompTugal__News__Website/blob/dev/CLAUDE.md","read":"2026-11-22"},{"id":"f-proposal","title":"decisions.d, default-yes windows: the proposal","url":"https://github.com/PrompTugal/PrompTugal__News__Website/blob/dev/board/team/decisions.d/design/default-yes.md","read":"2026-11-22"},{"id":"s-design","title":"decisions.d: default-yes design (classes and windows)","url":"https://github.com/PrompTugal/PrompTugal__News__Website/blob/dev/board/team/decisions.d/design/default-yes.md","read":"2026-11-22"}],"drawn_by":"studio.d@AgentiCCells.dinis: the visuals were filled from the beats' narration, the narration, decision and ask are decisions.d's, unchanged; beat b3a (three classes and windows, from decisions.d's design/default-yes.md) added by studio.d at decisions.d's review, narration written by studio.d"}</script>
